6	 * ## Why this is a step of its own
7	 *
8	 * The validation writes a check run and, when it can, dispatches an agent. When it
9	 * cannot, the check is still written and the work simply waits -- and a pull
10	 * request that waits unannounced is the failure this exists to prevent. It is the
11	 * same failure `unattendedNotice` covers at creation time, one round later: the
12	 * pull request was attended when it was opened, and the agent it named is not
13	 * coming because CI failed and the request came from a person.
14	 *
15	 * ## Who is told
16	 *
17	 * `resolveNotify`, which is the person who asked for the run -- the commenter for a
18	 * comment, the opener for an issue, and the repository owner as a last resort. It
19	 * is the same resolution every other notice uses, so a person who is told about a
20	 * failure here is the person who was told about the run starting.
21	 *
22	 * Usage:
23	 *   notify_unattended.ts --repo OWNER/REPO --number N --summary "..."
24	 */
